The mechanism is explicit in the repository, but an observable deployment impact requires runtime code to render or compare the experimental `unstable_Activity` value. The supplied context contains no usage data establishing that this occurs.

The experimental `unstable_Activity` element now has its own `react.activity` identity and reconciler work tag instead of being exported as the Offscreen type. Client reconciliation represents it as an Activity fiber wrapping an Offscreen child, server rendering sends it through the existing Offscreen path, and naming/DevTools logic recognizes it as `Activity`.

Likely behavioral changes
  • Callers importing `unstable_Activity` now receive the distinct global symbol `react.activity`, rather than the Offscreen element type. Identity comparisons and element construction using this export therefore distinguish Activity from Offscreen.
  • The client reconciler now accepts Activity as an element type, creates a dedicated Activity work item, and reconciles its children through an Offscreen child carrying the Activity `mode` and `children` properties.
  • During server rendering, Activity elements are handled by the same rendering path as Offscreen elements.
  • Fiber naming and DevTools inspection can now present the dedicated work tag as `Activity`, rather than treating the exported component solely as Offscreen.

